<article class="env-proposition" id="07PX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07PX">Proposition <span data-tag="07PX">15.51.12</span>.</a> The following types of rings are G-rings: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
fields, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Noetherian complete local rings, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathbf{Z}$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Dedekind domains with fraction field of characteristic zero, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
finite type ring extensions of any of the above. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      For fields, $\mathbf{Z}$ and Dedekind domains of characteristic zero this follows immediately from the definition and the fact that the completion of a discrete valuation ring is a discrete valuation ring. A Noetherian complete local ring is a G-ring by Proposition <a href="/tag/07PS" data-tag="07PS">15.51.6</a>. The statement on finite type overrings is Proposition <a href="/tag/07PV" data-tag="07PV">15.51.10</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>